## What is deliberately *not* included

- **No `dsh-go` APK, no decompiled dsh-go code, no dsh-go assets.** Chapter
  `docs/zh/07-reverse-engineering.md` only describes *interoperability facts*
  (process model, ports, config file layout) needed to make two apps on the same
  phone talk to each other. Reverse engineering for interoperability is
  documented; redistributing someone else's binary is not done here.
- **No credentials.** No API keys, no OAuth tokens, no subscription cookies. The
  gateway's local token is the literal string `magpie`, which is magpie's own
  documented loopback default, not a secret.
- **No signing key.** `keystore.jks` is git-ignored; each builder generates their
  own (see `docs/zh/02-build.md`). Release APKs are signed with the maintainer's
  key and carry the certificate fingerprint published in the release notes.

